@startuml client_send_queue_handle_reply_activity
title ClientSendQueue - handling a reply

start
:HandleReply(message);
:Lock lifetime_.mutex_;
if (Reply slot is disengaged or callback empty?) then (yes)
    :Unlock and return false;
    stop
else (no)
    :Move the callback locally;
endif
:Reset waiting_for_reply_ and clear its sender owner;
:DrainUnderLock(lock);
:Unlock lifetime_.mutex_;
:Invoke the completed callback with message;
:Return true;
stop

legend
    An empty drain or ordered-send marker is not a pending request callback.
    The facade maps false to unsolicited-reply kIoError stopping.
    Queued progress occurs before the completed callback is invoked.
    A later request may therefore own the slot before this callback runs.
endlegend

@enduml